================================================================================
RESEARCH SIGNIFICANCE
================================================================================

This module provides a complete dynamical description of tidal disruption
during the MW–M31 merger process.

While density analysis describes where matter exists and kinematic analysis
describes how particles move, this section investigates the physical
mechanisms responsible for structural transformation:

- gravitational stripping,
- tidal heating,
- debris formation,
- halo deformation,
- loss of gravitational binding,
- and morphological evolution.

The resulting diagnostics create a bridge between simulation particle
evolution and observable signatures expected from galaxy merger remnants.


